# SDL3.module's absolute references into its data, reviewed (tools/baserel_check.py),
# as for SDL2.module (library/modules/sdl2/baserel.allow). Each reaches the
# data as loaded, which no program's copy is; these are only ever read
# there, so every program sees the same first values. One regular
# expression a line, for the check's report line. Reviewed 22 October 2026.
#
# SDL_video.c's, SDL_audio.c's and SDL_camera.c's bootstrap[]: tables in the
# code of the back ends' VideoBootStrap/AudioBootStrap/CameraBootStrap (a
# name, a description and functions); SDL only reads them.
^table of _\w+_bootstrap \(.*\), from the code at .*\(SDL_(video|audio|camera)\.o\)\)$
# SDL_render.c's render_drivers[]: the software renderer's SDL_RenderDriver;
# SDL only reads it.
^table of _SW_RenderDriver \(.*\), from the code at .*\(SDL_render\.o\)\)$
# SDL_wave.c: its IMA ADPCM step table, a function's static const array,
# which GCC puts in the data and indexes from its absolute address.
^address of \.data\+0x0 of .*\(SDL_wave\.o\), from the code at .*\(SDL_wave\.o\)\)$
# SDL_assert.c: SDL_PromptAssertion's buttons[], a local array whose first
# values GCC keeps in the data and copies onto the stack.
^address of \.data\+0x0 of .*\(SDL_assert\.o\), from the code at .*\(SDL_assert\.o\)\)$
